{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Moses chose men of valor.</b> Men such as these, Moses was able to identify — the wealthy; but qualities of the heart, such as God-fearers, men of truth, haters of unjust gain — flesh and blood cannot see except by estimate of the mind. Therefore he did not mention them here, and also in Deuteronomy Moses did not mention them, only 'wise and discerning and known,' because these a person can identify in his fellow — whether he is wise or not — but a God-fearer he cannot identify."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:36.496777299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}